    """The run log's own border comparison (specs/0017-fuller-styles.md,
    "Harness runs", --border-sample and P2).
    
    Usage: bordercmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--plant <flag>]
           bordercmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads both archives with zipfile and ElementTree, sharing no code with the
    library or the tool, and makes its own pick of the edit --border-sample
    should have made, as fontcmp.py did for P1: the first worksheet in <sheets>
    order, A and M in it, and from the styles part X (the xf children of
    cellXfs), B (the border children of borders) and A's base, the xf A's s
    names (none when A has no s or there is no A).
    
    For the styles part, by byte spans:
    
      head_same         the bytes before <borders are the input's
      borders_xfs_gap   the bytes from </borders> to <cellXfs are the input's
      tail_same         the bytes from </cellXfs> to the end are the input's
      borders_prefix    inside borders, the input's children's bytes begin the
